description:
In repos/goal-host-vessel/src/index.ts, correct the HOLLOW summary so a beta withheld for symmetry is not reported as a beta that was applied.

Replace this exact line:
        tap(`[goal-host-vessel] walk(${opts.surface}): HOLLOW — ${verdict.reason}; ${_noOracle ? "β WITHHELD (no oracle owns this class)" : `β-penalised last pick ${lastPick}`}. completion_shapes=${JSON.stringify(verdict.completion_shapes)}`);

with this exact line:
        tap(`[goal-host-vessel] walk(${opts.surface}): HOLLOW — ${verdict.reason}; ${_noOracle ? "β WITHHELD (no oracle owns this class)" : _betaWithheldForSymmetry ? `β WITHHELD (α was structurally unreachable for ${lastPick} — symmetric abstention, not a penalty)` : `β-penalised last pick ${lastPick}`}. completion_shapes=${JSON.stringify(verdict.completion_shapes)}`);

Rationale from measurement: the branch above this line already withholds beta whenever _betaWithheldForSymmetry is true, and it does so correctly. This summary line distinguishes only the _noOracle case, so a symmetry-withheld beta prints as "β-penalised last pick". Over ten dispatches that line asserted 12 penalties while the authoritative learning sink recorded alphaBetaDelta of [] on every one of them; zero penalties were applied. Two published conclusions about this system's learning dynamics were drawn from those lines and both were wrong. The comment immediately above records the same defect being found and repaired once already for the sibling branch, noting that the log is what the reach-gate lessons, the judge, and every after-the-fact analysis read. A second withholding branch was introduced later and this line was never widened to cover it.

